<div class=mywhitetext>
<h3>Guild Ranks<o:p></o:p></h3>

<h4>Warlord<o:p></o:p></h4>

<p>The Warlord oversees the entire guild process. The Warlord will obtain
weekly verbal reports from the Circle of Bones as to the status of the various
Battalions, any new recruits/disbands, and any issues (both good and bad) that
have arisen. The Warlord is <u>the final stage</u> in all guild issues. All
issues should be handled via the ranking system within Bloodhorde. However, if
an issue is of unusual importance, it can be brought to the immediate attention
of the Warlord.<o:p></o:p></p>

<p><b>Circle of Bones</b><o:p></o:p></p>

<p>The Circle of Bones takes over the responsibilities of the Warlord when the
Warlord is not present. The Circle of Bones have the power to make emergency
guild decisions when the Warlord is not present. However, no one Circle of
Bones officer can make a decision alone. Any decision must be seconded by
another Circle of Bones member. Of course if there are no other Circle of Bones
members available and the issue is time critical, the officer may make a
judgment call. However, if the issue can wait until another officer or the
Warlord is available, they should wait to consult with the other officers.<o:p></o:p></p>

<p>Responsibilities of the the Circle of Bones:<o:p></o:p></p>

<ol start=1 type=1>
 <li class=MsoNormal style='mso-margin-top-alt:auto;mso-margin-bottom-alt:auto;
     mso-list:l3 level1 lfo1;tab-stops:list .5in'>External Liaison - All
     officers of the Circle of Bones have the responsibility of handling
     non-Bloodhorde issues. This includes external complaints about the
     Bloodhorde or our members. It also includes maintaining relations with
     other guilds/individuals for raids, guild wars, etc. <o:p></o:p></li>
 <li class=MsoNormal style='mso-margin-top-alt:auto;mso-margin-bottom-alt:auto;
     mso-list:l3 level1 lfo1;tab-stops:list .5in'>Final step in dealing with
     internal issues (personal complaints, conflicts between Bloodhorde
     members, etc.). If necessary, the Warlord may be contacted to finalize the
     situation. <o:p></o:p></li>
 <li class=MsoNormal style='mso-margin-top-alt:auto;mso-margin-bottom-alt:auto;
     mso-list:l3 level1 lfo1;tab-stops:list .5in'>Raid Planning - The Circle of
     Bones will help in raid planning by discussing the raid plan and goals
     with the Raid Commander <o:p></o:p></li>
</ol>

<p><b>Blood Knight</b><o:p></o:p></p>

<p>Members of the Blood Knight rank are appointed by the Circle of Bones. The
main responsibilities of the Blood Knights include:<o:p></o:p></p>

<ol start=1 type=1>
 <li class=MsoNormal style='mso-margin-top-alt:auto;mso-margin-bottom-alt:auto;
     mso-list:l4 level1 lfo2;tab-stops:list .5in'>Battalion Management - Three
     Blood Knights will be assigned to oversee all functions of a Battalion.
     The Knight has the power to tell a battalion where to hunt, or specify
     goals for the battalion (we need items from X zone, the battalion is
     lacking xp growth so hunt at X zone) if necessary. The Blood Knight is not
     there to command a battalion, but rather to help guide them to make them
     most efficient. <o:p></o:p></li>
 <li class=MsoNormal style='mso-margin-top-alt:auto;mso-margin-bottom-alt:auto;
     mso-list:l4 level1 lfo2;tab-stops:list .5in'>Report any Battalion issues
     to the Circle of Bones at least weekly in an email report. If any issue is
     severe, it should be reported immediately to the Circle of Bones. <o:p></o:p></li>
</ol>

<p><b>Bone Guard</b><o:p></o:p></p>

<p>Three Bone Guard will assigned to oversee a specific battalion. They are the
first in line when the battalion Dragoon or Crusader cannot resolve an issue.
(Personal conflict, etc.). Responsibilities include:<o:p></o:p></p>

<ol start=1 type=1>
 <li class=MsoNormal style='mso-margin-top-alt:auto;mso-margin-bottom-alt:auto;
     mso-list:l2 level1 lfo3;tab-stops:list .5in'>Assisting the Battalion
     Dragoons and Crusaders with advice when needed <o:p></o:p></li>
 <li class=MsoNormal style='mso-margin-top-alt:auto;mso-margin-bottom-alt:auto;
     mso-list:l2 level1 lfo3;tab-stops:list .5in'>Second Stage of Battalion
     issues. If the Battalion Dragoon/Crusader are unable to handle an issue
     that has arisen in their battalion, they should contact a Bone Guard to
     help resolve the situation. <o:p></o:p></li>
</ol>

<h4>Horde Member<o:p></o:p></h4>

<p>This is the standard membership rank of Bloodhorde. Although a Horde Member
does not have authority within the guild, they still have responsibilities.
These responsibilities include:<o:p></o:p></p>

<ol start=1 type=1>
 <li class=MsoNormal style='mso-margin-top-alt:auto;mso-margin-bottom-alt:auto;
     mso-list:l1 level1 lfo4;tab-stops:list .5in'>Set an outstanding example.
     When you are out in the world of Norrath, your actions reflect not only
     upon yourself, but also upon the guild. All members need to remember that
     Bloodhorde is an honorable guild and we do not get involved in childish or
     petty situations. <o:p></o:p></li>
 <li class=MsoNormal style='mso-margin-top-alt:auto;mso-margin-bottom-alt:auto;
     mso-list:l1 level1 lfo4;tab-stops:list .5in'>Help initiate new Minion
     recruits. New members may be unfamiliar with Bloodhorde rules and/or
     procedures. If you see a member that is not following the Bloodhorde
     rules, send them a private tell and help clarify things for them. If the
     situation is severe (the new member is being extremely rude, etc) you
     should privately contact a ranking member to help resolve the situation. <o:p></o:p></li>
</ol>

<p><b>Blood Minion</b><o:p></o:p></p>

<p>This is the rank that all alternate characters of Horde Members are
assigned. They have all the same responsibilities as that of a character of
Horde Member rank. This is the highest rank an alternate character can hold.<o:p></o:p></p>

<p><b>Minion</b><o:p></o:p></p>

<p>When a new member is tagged as part of Bloodhorde, they are inducted as a
Minion of Bloodhorde. Minions have some basic responsibilities that include:<o:p></o:p></p>

<ol start=1 type=1>
 <li class=MsoNormal style='mso-margin-top-alt:auto;mso-margin-bottom-alt:auto;
     mso-list:l0 level1 lfo5;tab-stops:list .5in'>Set an outstanding example.
     When you are out in the world of Norrath, your actions reflect not only
     upon yourself, but also upon the guild. All members need to remember that
     Bloodhorde is an honorable guild and we do not get involved in childish or
     petty situations. <o:p></o:p></li>
 <li class=MsoNormal style='mso-margin-top-alt:auto;mso-margin-bottom-alt:auto;
     mso-list:l0 level1 lfo5;tab-stops:list .5in'>Learn the Bloodhorde rules
     and procedures. The way Bloodhorde operates could be significantly
     different from other guilds you may have been in. Make sure you read and
     understand the guild rules. Doing so will help you understand who we are
     and hopefully make us much more fun to be with. <o:p></o:p></li>
</ol>

<p class=MsoNormal><![if !supportEmptyParas]>&nbsp;<![endif]><o:p></o:p></p>

